    note: "⛔ FOUND WHILE ANSWERING A DIFFERENT QUESTION, by scanning every contract obligation that is MECHANICALLY checkable against the live saves. Everything else came back clean — 50 choices with 0 invalid subAttributes, 0 unknown or unowned abilityIds, 0 out-of-band difficulties, 0 unresolvable encounter/emergence ids, 110 NPCs with 0 invalid statuses and 0 duplicate ids for one human. The single finding: 35 of 110 registered people carry NEITHER gender NOR pronouns, despite the GM contract marking it REQUIRED on meet — so roughly a third of the people a player has met have their portrait gender guessed, which is SNG-143 (Pell rendered male) from the other end. ⚠️ THE ENGINE'S OWN BACKFILL IS CORRECT AND IS NOT THE GAP: `backfillNpcGender` stamps only where a record's own prose is unambiguous (two or more pronouns, and at least double the other) and REFUSES to guess otherwise — which is right, and leaves exactly these 35. The gap is authored, not computed. ⛔ AND THE REPAIR TOOL COULD NOT REACH THEM ALL: the control read `.slice(0, 30)` in registry order while Silas knows 34 people, so four were unreachable with nothing on screen to say so — and being registry-ordered, the four dropped were the most RECENTLY met, i.e. precisely the people just seen rendered wrong. That is the codex `slice(-40)` lesson wearing a different hat: a cap on a LOG is housekeeping, a cap on a REPAIR is a repair you cannot perform. It now lists everyone, unrecorded first, and states the count.",
